        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e718cd87-7d38-57cc-b959-355b589a0257",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Innocence Mission, Starflyer 59\n- People: Karen Peris, Don Peris, Mike Bitts, Steve Brown, Jason Martin, Ronnie Martin\n- Places: Lancaster, Pennsylvania, Riverside, California\n- Genres: Folk rock, alternative rock\n- Events: Catholic school production of \"Godspell\"\n\nFacts:\n- The Innocence Mission was formed in Lancaster, Pennsylvania in the early 1980s after its members met during a Catholic school production of \"Godspell\".\n- The Innocence Mission is an American folk rock band centered on husband-and-wife singer-songwriters Karen Peris and Don Peris, and its lineup also includes Mike Bitts on bass guitar and Steve Brown on drums.\n- Since 1995, The Innocence Mission has stylized its name as \"the innocence mission\" on all releases.\n- Starflyer 59 is an alternative rock band from Riverside, California.\n- Starflyer 59 was founded in 1993 by Jason Martin, who is the brother of Ronnie Martin of Joy Electric.",
